    "## Lesson 1: Introduction to RAG"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Welcome to the RAG Tutorial!\n",
    "\n",
    "This tutorial will guide you through building **Retrieval-Augmented Generation** (RAG) systems â€” one of the most practical and powerful architectural patterns for working with large language models today."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What You'll Learn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "By the end of this tutorial, you'll be able to:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Understand what RAG is and why it matters\n",
    "2. Build simple and advanced RAG systems using LangChain\n",
    "3. Process and chunk documents effectively\n",
    "4. Create vector databases for semantic search\n",
    "5. Build production-ready RAG applications\n",
    "6. Evaluate and optimize your RAG systems\n",
    "7. Deploy a end-to-end PDF document Q&A system"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What is Retrieval-Augmented Generation?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The Basic Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "RAG is a pattern that **combines** traditional retrieval systems (like search engines) with large language models. Instead of just generating answers from pre-trained knowledge, the model:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Takes a user question\n",
    "2. Searches an external knowledge base for relevant information\n",
    "3. Uses that retrieved context to generate a more accurate, grounded answer\n",
    "\n",
    "**The pipeline:** Query â†’ Retrieve â†’ Combine â†’ Generate â†’ Answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A Simple Diagram"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Traditional LLM Approach âŒ\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "â”Œâ”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”     â”Œâ”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”\n",
    "â”‚   User Query    â”‚  â†’  â”‚   LLM              â”‚\n",
    "â”‚  \"Who founded   â”‚     â”‚  (only has         â”‚\n",
    "â”‚   Microsoft?)\"  â”‚     â”‚  training data)     â”‚\n",
    "â””â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”˜     â””â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”˜\n",
    "                           â”‚\n",
    "                           â–¼\n",
    "                    \"I think Bill Gates...\"\n",
    "                    \"or maybe Paul Allen...\"\n",
    "                    \"(Maybe he founded it?)\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "*Problem: Model hallucinates or relies only on training data cutoff*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RAG Approach âœ…\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "â”Œâ”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”  â”Œâ”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”  â”Œâ”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”\n",
    "â”‚   User Query    â”‚  â”‚   Document   â”‚  â”‚   LLM           â”‚\n",
    "â”‚  \"Who founded   â”‚ â†’â”‚   Search     â”‚ â†’â”‚  (has           â”‚\n",
    "â”‚   Microsoft?)\"  â”‚  â”‚ Engine /     â”‚  â”‚  context +      â”‚\n",
    "â””â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”˜  â”‚   Vector DB  â”‚  â”‚  retrieval      â”‚\n",
    "                     â””â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”˜  â”‚  data)          â”‚\n",
    "                                       â””â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”˜\n",
    "                           â”‚                 â”‚\n",
    "                           â–¼                 â–¼\n",
    "                    \"Bill Gates founded \n",
    "                     Microsoft in 1975. \n",
    "                     According to our records...\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "*Benefit: Factual, up-to-date, grounded answers*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Traditional LLMs vs RAG: Key Differences"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "| Aspect | Traditional LLM | RAG |\n",
    "|--------|-----------------|-----|\n",
    "| **Knowledge Source** | Pre-trained only | External knowledge base |\n",
    "| **Updates** | Requires retraining | Add documents instantly |\n",
    "| **Accuracy** | Can hallucinate | Grounded in facts |\n",
    "| **Domain Specificity** | General knowledge | Can specialize |\n",
    "| **Citations** | Rarely provides them | Can cite sources |\n",
    "| **Cost** | API calls â†’ $$$ | Depends on storage/retrieval |\n",
    "| **Latency** | Fast | Slightly slower (retrieval step) |\n",
    "| **Context Length** | Limited (~128K) | Can grow as needed |\n",
    "| **Data Privacy** | External API | Self-hosted option |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why RAG? Benefits and Use Cases"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Benefits\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Reduced Hallucinations**: Answers are grounded in retrieved documents\n",
    "2. **Up-to-date Information**: No need to retrain; just add new docs\n",
    "3. **Domain Specificity**: Customize for any industry or use case\n",
    "4. **Explainability**: Can show sources and evidence for answers\n",
    "5. **Cost Efficiency**: Less API calls when context is well-retrieved\n",
    "6. **Data Privacy**: Can use self-hosted models and documents"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Common Use Cases\n",
    "\n",
    "| Use Case | Description |\n",
    "|----------|------------|\n",
    "| **Company Knowledge Base** | Q&A about internal docs, policies, employee handbooks |\n",
    "| **Customer Support** | Automated support with company documentation |\n",
    "| **Research Assistant** | Summarize academic papers, find research gaps |\n",
    "| **Legal Tech** | Research case law, find relevant precedents |\n",
    "| **Healthcare** | Query medical guidelines and patient records |\n",
    "| **Code Documentation** | Query codebase, find usage examples |\n",
    "| **E-commerce** | Product information, recommendations |\n",
    "| **Personal Knowledge Management** | Your notes, bookmarks, documents in one place |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Real-World Examples"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Example 1: Corporate FAQ Bot\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scenario**: Employees ask questions about company policies, benefits, or onboarding\n",
    "\n",
    "**How RAG works**:\n",
    "- Store all HR handbooks, policy docs, and FAQs\n",
    "- Employee asks: \"How do I apply for parental leave?\"\n",
    "- RAG retrieves relevant policy sections\n",
    "- LLM generates answer citing source documents\n",
    "\n",
    "**Impact**: 24/7 support, reduced HR workload, consistent answers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Example 2: Legal Research Tool\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scenario**: Lawyers need to find relevant case law and precedents\n",
    "\n",
    "**How RAG works**:\n",
    "- Index thousands of court judgments and legal opinions\n",
    "- Lawyer queries: \"What's the ruling on breach of contract in California?\"\n",
    "- RAG retrieves most relevant cases\n",
    "- LLM summarizes and highlights key legal points\n",
    "\n",
    "**Impact**: Faster research, better-informed strategy, documented reasoning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Example 3: Technical Documentation AI\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scenario**: Internal software docs are scattered across wikis\n",
    "\n",
    "**How RAG works**:\n",
    "- Ingest Confluence, Notion, GitHub docs\n",
    "- Engineers ask: \"How do I configure environment variables for deployment?\"\n",
    "- RAG finds relevant docs across multiple sources\n",
    "- LLM synthesizes step-by-step instructions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Impact**: Reduced documentation churn, faster onboarding, less context switching"
   ]
  },
